# Vendored pdf.js build — bundled so cached PDFs open OFFLINE on Android.
#
# These are third-party build artifacts, not our source. The repo runs with
# core.autocrlf=true, which would rewrite the line endings INSIDE a 377KB /
# 1.1MB minified JavaScript file on every checkout — changing the bytes we
# verified against the official pdfjs-dist tarball, and differing between a
# Windows dev machine and the Linux EAS build machine. Mark them binary so git
# never transforms them: what we vetted is exactly what ships.
frontend/assets/pdfjs/pdf.min.txt        -text
frontend/assets/pdfjs/pdf.worker.min.txt -text

# Test fixtures whose bytes are compared and hashed. core.autocrlf=true
# checks them out CRLF on Windows, so the file a test ran on and the blob
# that was committed hashed differently (2026-09-22, #650). LF everywhere.
backend/tests/ocr_grid_tables.json   text eol=lf
backend/tests/discipline_corpus.json text eol=lf
